{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules","id":854902,"title":"ire and the rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-29T00:08:57-07:00","id":854902,"title":"ire and the rules","content":"hi dudes and dudettes.<br /> <br /> If vampire is a great game, the rules of the game are Heavy. It 's one of the most onerous rule in the modern RPG world. My problem, i lost too much players, they prefer playing game with more easy rule like deadlans reloaded, D&amp;D, Cthullu.<br /> <br /> My question is, can we hope to see one day a vampire version with simple and fast rules ?<br /> <br /> Thx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11521-saerdryl","name":"saerdryl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T00:20:27-07:00","id":854906,"title":"","content":"Well a quick start guide got released back in the day that had some fast and dirty rules in it.<br /> <br /> Apart from that you can feel free to use or not use whatever rules you want from the main book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T00:36:51-07:00","id":854908,"title":"","content":"I know it but when u pla, u throw too much dice.... D20 system, D 100..... are faster and easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11521-saerdryl","name":"saerdryl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T00:45:19-07:00","id":854910,"title":"","content":"It's a D10 system, Monte' Cooks world of darkness is d20 based but I don't know how easily Requiem ports into it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons! 03-29-2016, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:32:11-07:00","id":854945,"title":"","content":"How the crap D&amp;D is more rules light than CofD with all the charts and shit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:17:25-07:00","id":854981,"title":"","content":"I think he's asking for a quickstart pamphlet or download but he said easier rules and fewer dice. (Certainly not true re: dice with D&amp;D since different weapons and spells use a different sided dice.) He's right, over the years, CoD has become one of the most byzantine RPG systems currently on the market that caters primarily to a pre-existing fan base, while most RPG lines are designed or redesigned to appeal to people who's first RPG experience came from a first person shooter on XBox on Playstation with little to no prior experience with pen and paper games. I know the current and several previous editions of D&amp;D the rules are contained in one book but you still have to buy multiple books for CoD. The charts are also easier to consult but you have to dig all over the place and in multiple books for CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:27:15-07:00","id":854988,"title":"","content":"All I know is that CofD assumes the ST's prominence in all manners of rulings, D&amp;D tries to provide specific rulings that simply fall apart the moment you begin to check spell interactions.<br /> <br /> 2E does what it intents extremely well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:32:46-07:00","id":855090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=854945#post854945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the crap D&amp;D is more rules light than CofD with all the charts and shit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I totally agree with this. ^<br /> <br /> I learned to play dnd when there was THAC0 ... If that right there wasnt more complicated than all of Wod.. I dont know what is. Ok ok..I exaggerate. But Dungeons and dragons was really rule intensive and way more math. I played 3.5 weekly with my group for years. there are 30 some books 50 some classes... with vampires there are 5 clans. That Right there it is easier. You add a skill points to every roll. there is a lot of adding, same in Vampire. If you dont want to actually be rolling 10-15 dice and counting the successes. There are a lot of great apps that do it for you and make the dice rolling way easier than dnd's dice. ( story teller dice app for iphone is great)<br /> <br /> <br /> DND for example my fighter would roll 8 D20 and Add.. +20/+15/+10/+5 ( + all sorts of other bonuses ) then once i know I hit.. i would start rolling all the D10s and adding all sorts of other d6s or whatevers... <br /> <br /> <br /> Sometimes having someone teach you the game helps a lot. a couple of years ago my group wanted to switch from dnd to a vampire /werewolf cross over and I was super resistant to it. Actually the only one who didnt want to, but after some coaching I find it way easier than DnD both from a ST and PLayer point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:49:50-07:00","id":855097,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D 5th edition is a pretty streamlined system, actually. Some of their big design goals included a very simple baseline with knobs to increase complexity for those that wanted it, character creation that could be done in 10 minutes, and combats that could be done in 10 minutes.<br /> <br /> ...Aaaaaanywhoo, I agree with Tsusai, CofD is a rules-medium system by default that can be adjusted for more or less complexity based on which subsystems you chose to employ or not to employ. But it's designed for people who are already familiar with TTRPGs. If I was introducing a new player to tabletop gaming, I would much sooner use D&amp;D 5e than CofD to show them the ropes (though, depending on their age I might even sooner use Pugmire).<br /> <br /> And that's not a bad thing, in my opinion! A lot of tabletop RPGs have shifted their focus lately to ease of use for new players, where CofD is one of the few that still caters to those of us who have been involved in the hobby for a while. It's good to have both options out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:10:40-07:00","id":855106,"title":"","content":"My first RPG ever was Geist and I got the hang of it just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:18:51-07:00","id":855109,"title":"","content":"Sure, but obviously the OP and their group is struggling with vampire, and frankly I don't blame them. There's a lot in there to learn, and while it's easy for those of us familiar to the system to say &quot;all these parts are optional, you can pare it down if you need&quot;, it takes a certain degree of system mastery to know what can and can't be cut and what the greater implications will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:24:03-07:00","id":855111,"title":"","content":"My group is playing 5th now. It is a lot easier than 3.5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=855109#post855109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but obviously the OP and their group is struggling with vampire, and frankly I don't blame them. There's a lot in there to learn, and while it's easy for those of us familiar to the system to say &quot;all these parts are optional, you can pare it down if you need&quot;, it takes a certain degree of system mastery to know what can and can't be cut and what the greater implications will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>A coach could help with that or someone to verbally explain certain elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:38:10-07:00","id":855118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=854945#post854945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the crap D&amp;D is more rules light than CofD with all the charts and shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out 5th edition and you'll find! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The combat section in the PHB is 10 pages. No charts, no grid (albeit it is in the DMG as an <i>optional </i>thing with some other things). At this time, ironicaly CofD/WoD has more simlationist rules and weapons and other charts than DnD. Actualy, 5th ed is very rules-light, hence the great success and massive flood of new players. Just 2 weeks ago, here in Hungary, Budapest, we had a 5E competiton day (with the option to playing in a casual group), with 100+ participiants. And it was always troublesome to gather people outside of the translated, or native rpgs, so it surprised me big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=854988#post854988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that CofD assumes the ST's prominence in all manners of rulings, D&amp;D tries to provide specific rulings that simply fall apart the moment you begin to check spell interactions.<br /> <br /> 2E does what it intents extremely well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, some of 5E's biggest statements are &quot;rulings, not rules&quot;, and using the &quot;ask the DM&quot; sentence a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm planning to start a WoD, or CofD chronicle (still struggling between Requiem and Ascension) with some of my friends who never played RPGs and after some inner debating I concluded that we will start with plain vanilla humans and I'll lend them as much support as I can and add the supernatural splats much later and from point zero (total neonates, or apprentice mages), because no way, <i>no way </i>they would read all the rules and understand them. It is too much. So I will start with the most simple and trying to hook them and then teach them the splat powers rules on the fly, integrated into the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 03-29-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T10:52:06-07:00","id":855132,"title":"","content":"I have the player's handbook, the monster's book and the Master's guide for 5e. It took me a week, as a player, to set my character's spellbook. I don't recall reading &quot;ask the DM&quot; in a single spell description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T11:19:04-07:00","id":855141,"title":"","content":"Cutting down the rules to the basics shouldn't be too hard. Use Quick and Dirty for combat, don't use the 'feeding scenes' and social system with the Doors, and just RP it. There's probably simplified ritual rules. Other than basic actions, Disciplines and Humanity there isn't much I can think of, offhand, that requires rolls and happens often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=855106#post855106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first RPG ever was Geist and I got the hang of it just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now <i>that's </i>surprising. And it got you interested in the rest of the World of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T11:27:43-07:00","id":855147,"title":"","content":"Problem with CoD rules more often lies im their presentation than in actual engine. Its often hard to find the rules you need and they often are hidden in unintuitive places.<br /> For the op - try playing with a diceroller. Properly set up script can accelerate the play to the sky, because pretty much majority of the rolls can be set up as &quot;roll a pool, icheck if there is st least one 8 9 10&quot;. Use less contested rolls and more simple rolls with penalties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:01:13-07:00","id":855162,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the core resolution system for CofD is super simple. Pick an Attribute and a second Attribute or Skill, add up the dots, apply bonuses or penalties, roll that many d10s. If you get an 8, a 9, or a 10, the action succeeds, if not it fails. Pretty much everything beyond that is optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:03:44-07:00","id":855165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=855141#post855141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now <i>that's </i>surprising. And it got you interested in the rest of the World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there was some other stuff. I got roped in to run a Vampire game because I knew the system and it blossomed from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:19:57-07:00","id":855175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=855132#post855132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the player's handbook, the monster's book and the Master's guide for 5e. It took me a week, as a player, to set my character's spellbook. I don't recall reading &quot;ask the DM&quot; in a single spell description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not <i>literally, </i>but, here you go, from the Wish's description: &quot;Vou might be able to achieve something beyond the scope of the above examples. State your wish to the DM as precisely as possible. The DM has great latitude in ruling what occurs in such an instance; the greater the wish, the greater the Iikelihood that something goes wrong.&quot; Aside, most spells don't need to state &quot;ask the DM&quot;, because they have exact effects (like, for example, disciplines). Weapons, or tools also don't have to.<br /> <br /> I could cite a lot of examples from either the PHB or DMG, but I think it would be futile. If you read them and still don' think 5E is rules light or put great emphasis on the DM empowerment compared to earlier editions, well, probably I can't say anything that could sway your opinion. The overall majority definitely hold that yes it is and yes it did.<br /> <br /> CofD is very simple on the surface, add together points, pick up dices, roll, count 8+s. BUT, it has a lot of additional rules especially the splats. It's much better than for example DnD 3e, or PF, but I think Charlaquin nailed it, it's rules-medium, while 5E is indeed rules-light. I know it's strange to a player, who came from earlier editions to Wod, or CofD, but here it is. It also helps that the naure of the leveling system of DnD makes possible to start with very little &quot;have to know&quot;, and feats and multiclassing are optional.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:30:55-07:00","id":855182,"title":"","content":"I think CofD also has an easier learning curve if you start out playing normal humans, then transition to a splat if you are so inclined after you've got the basics down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:06:29-07:00","id":855311,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Humans don't have too much super special rules going for them; pretty much everything you have to learn is something about *systems you use*, not *inherent power of your splat*. Humans roll dice, and that's it. Anything special comes in form of merits and subsystems that can be ignored. <br /> Splats, on the other hand, expect you to assimilate a lot of exceptions to the default state, special interactions, special quirks, special rules, special abilities and in general, a lot of specific information that isn't intuitive. And biggest problem here is that usually, these things are spelled out...over the course of a whole book. If you are uninterested in all the fluff (and that's valid! I usually read it once and never again, because I don't really care; I know people who never read the fluff, only the game rules), you are going to have a bad day trying to learn and understand &quot;here are all the little things you are expected to know about your splat&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:35:32-07:00","id":860754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saerdryl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules#post854902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hi dudes and dudettes.<br /> <br /> If vampire is a great game, the rules of the game are Heavy. It 's one of the most onerous rule in the modern RPG world. My problem, i lost too much players, they prefer playing game with more easy rule like deadlans reloaded, D&amp;D, Cthullu.<br /> <br /> My question is, can we hope to see one day a vampire version with simple and fast rules ?<br /> <br /> Thx</div> </div> </div> </div>Is rolling multiple dice the only problem? Or are there other things your group is not grokking? Let's break this down.<br /> <br /> No offense but Requiem may not be light but it aint heavy. Try Chivalry &amp; Sorcery or Rolemaster(AKA Rules master). One version of Empire of the Petal Throne had an 8 page character sheet which included a tax form. I shit you not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:54:08-07:00","id":860758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=854981#post854981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he's asking for a quickstart pamphlet or download but he said easier rules and fewer dice. (Certainly not true re: dice with D&amp;D since different weapons and spells use a different sided dice.) He's right, over the years, CoD has become one of the most byzantine RPG systems currently on the market that caters primarily to a pre-existing fan base, while most RPG lines are designed or redesigned to appeal to people who's first RPG experience came from a first person shooter on XBox on Playstation with little to no prior experience with pen and paper games. I know the current and several previous editions of D&amp;D the rules are contained in one book but you still have to buy multiple books for CoD. The charts are also easier to consult but you have to dig all over the place and in multiple books for CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the CofD assumption is that you only need one rule book. Everything else is optional modules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:56:11-07:00","id":860760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860754#post860754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is rolling multiple dice the only problem? Or are there other things your group is not grokking? Let's break this down.<br /> <br /> No offense but Requiem may not be light but it aint heavy. Try Chivalry &amp; Sorcery or Rolemaster(AKA Rules master). One version of Empire of the Petal Throne had an 8 page character sheet which included a tax form. I shit you not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me that Hero (famously known for Champions) is still out there. It's so heavy (complex) that you need software to make characters. (So many Arcane maths.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T22:06:27-07:00","id":860788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860754#post860754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is rolling multiple dice the only problem? Or are there other things your group is not grokking? Let's break this down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you imagine that complain with Exalted? Heheheh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:52:41-07:00","id":860900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860758#post860758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the CofD assumption is that you only need one rule book. Everything else is optional modules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. You need the God Machine Chronicles book, you need whatever splat (singular or plural) that you're playing, and you will need whatever first edition book that second edition book references. In the case of 2nd edition Vampire, you need Blood Sorcery. You need a computer, tablet, or cell phone with internet access to check for erratas (and a printer to print them out) and/or you have to buy the PDF version of everything and routinely check to make sure it's updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:34:23-07:00","id":860913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860900#post860900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. You need the God Machine Chronicles book, you need whatever splat (singular or plural) that you're playing, and you will need whatever first edition book that second edition book references. In the case of 2nd edition Vampire, you need Blood Sorcery. You need a computer, tablet, or cell phone with internet access to check for erratas (and a printer to print them out) and/or you have to buy the PDF version of everything and routinely check to make sure it's updated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have a point there if anything you just said was true. You need the splat book. <i>Literally everything else you listed</i> is in the splat book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-07-2016, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:42:54-07:00","id":860948,"title":"","content":"Nothing listed is in the splatbook. That's, presumably, why it was listed by tsusasi. I actually really resent the design decision to try and stuff everything into the splatbooks. They failed. Tons of important rules still require the bluebook core. They aren't in the splatbooks. And instead of using word count for stuff that actually matters, it gets wasted on repeating half the bluebook core over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:53:49-07:00","id":860958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860760#post860760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This reminds me that Hero (famously known for Champions) is still out there. It's so heavy (complex) that you need software to make characters. (So many Arcane maths.)</div> </div> </div> </div> just another tool kit kit system.<br /> <br /> I never needed software. Basic arithmetic. What is arcane about that? Not like traveller with its ship vectors.<br /> Or D&amp; D 3 or 4 with all the specialists snowflake prestige classes scattered across gawd knows how many books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:15:56-07:00","id":860972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860948#post860948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tons of important rules still require the bluebook core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as? It's cut down a bit, but nothing you really <i>need</i> is left out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:20:07-07:00","id":860976,"title":"","content":"I think the rules of CofD are pretty good: they aren't too heavy and in the meantime they cover a lot of situations and offer a guide to resolve a wide range of actions, more or less complex, that other game systems don't touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:10:13-07:00","id":861164,"title":"","content":"I still want to hear from OP and help with their issues. BTW are they playing first or second editon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:13:00-07:00","id":861165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860900#post860900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. You need the God Machine Chronicles book, you need whatever splat (singular or plural) that you're playing, and you will need whatever first edition book that second edition book references. In the case of 2nd edition Vampire, you need Blood Sorcery. You need a computer, tablet, or cell phone with internet access to check for erratas (and a printer to print them out) and/or you have to buy the PDF version of everything and routinely check to make sure it's updated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Untrue. You simply need one core book. <br /> <br /> Want to play humans? Chronicles of Darkness will work.<br /> <br /> Vampires? Use Vampire: the Requiem 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Demons? See Demon: the Descent (revised ed.)<br /> <br /> Werewolves? Just grab a copy of Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd ed. <br /> <br /> etc., etc.<br /> <br /> These are all sandbox games, nothing gets hurt if your personal copy isn't &quot;up to date&quot; or you choose not to use stuff. You only need extra books when you choose to add stuff that isn't in one of the cores. Added stuff == optional stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:21:03-07:00","id":861170,"title":"","content":"Demon currently requires two books. I'm not sure if there are any plans to release a &quot;complete&quot; edition, although that would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:44:34-07:00","id":861181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860958#post860958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> just another tool kit kit system.<br /> <br /> I never needed software. Basic arithmetic. What is arcane about that? Not like traveller with its ship vectors.<br /> Or D&amp; D 3 or 4 with all the specialists snowflake prestige classes scattered across gawd knows how many books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, you never loaded up any powers with multiple advantages and limitations. The math crunch (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hero_System#Mathematics_issues\" target=\"_blank\">see here</a>) is the definition of heavy weight crunch. That software made character creation loads easier.<br /> <br /> I am noticing a trend in some of the comments though. Is your idea of &quot;heavy&quot; the use of multiple (always totally optional) books how you're defining it? I mean I get that from that point of view D&amp;D in all of its incarnations is relatively heavy because you need at least 2 of 3 core books to run it but I always found it to be rules lighter than Hero which has such a mathed out combat system that you basically play a miniatures board game every time combat happens. Personally I'm of the opinion that D&amp;D 3.5 and 2 are both (to use some boxing analogies) Super-middleweight systems compared to things like Rolemaster (Cruiserweight) and Hero System (Heavyweight). Compared to those systems CofD is a pretty svelt Middleweight system. Now D&amp;D 5 might be a Welterweight system but it had a few idiosyncracies I didn't like so there was no reason to update my personal version of 3.5 to it. If you want to see some lightweight systems, check out the Amber Diceless RPG sometime. The thing is like a Super-flyweight. And keep in mind that we're talking about actual crunchy bits. The engines under the hood. If you measure is something like book count then D&amp;D in all of its incarnations takes the cake, followed by the New World of Darkness (now often referred to as CofD 1e). You should also realize though that the need for all of those books was a revenue strategy on the old WWP company's part (regarding nWoD). If you need more books, you buy more books, so corporate profit = more. That doesn't have anything to do with overall game quality and uptake per se though.<br /> <br /> You should also realize that extra books are exactly that, extra. No one's holding a gun to your head and telling you to use them or buy them. IMO, trying to collect them all (like they're Piokemon) and employ them all at once is as silly as using all of the Arkham Horror or Talisman expansions at the same time. Neither of those games are actually designed for that type of play (and so the expansion themes necessary get diluted). If you're worried about some pundit here quoting esoteric passages from this book or that, don't. (We're all overblown windbags.) All that matters is that you and your troupe enjoy the experience of whatever game you're playing. Feel free to use as much or as little of just those books you need to to run the game you want to. After all, sandbox play is one of the primary features differentiating CofD from WoD.<br /> <br /> Also, on the topic of Hero System--that's an enjoyable system. It's my preferred go-to system for superhero-style games. That said I've ported things like Warhammer, Warhammer 40k, and Shadowrun into it. Partially because I thought they ran better in it and partially because I could. (I'm like that guy who lives down the street from you who's building a Lamborgini from scratch in his garage. He might not be the engineer who designed it but he knows things about its capabilities that the inventor never even dreamed of. Pulling games apart and putting them back together is something I do for fun. I've been doing it for about 30 years now, so I'm really, really good at it.)<br /> <br /> If Vampire is what you want to play, just get the 2e core book. You don't need anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 04-07-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:46:42-07:00","id":861183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=861170#post861170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon currently requires two books. I'm not sure if there are any plans to release a &quot;complete&quot; edition, although that would be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does it? I could swear everything necessary to play appears in Appendix 2 (aka &quot;The God-Machine Rules update&quot;).<br /> <br /> EDIT: That said, I wouldn't mind if someone hired a summer layouts intern to rearrange its content to better align with the stylings of the other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 04-07-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:28:04-07:00","id":861255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=861181#post861181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol, you never loaded up any powers with multiple advantages and limitations. The math crunch (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hero_System#Mathematics_issues\" target=\"_blank\">see here</a>) is the definition of heavy weight crunch. That software made character creation loads easier.<br /> <br /> I am noticing a trend in some of the comments though. Is your idea of &quot;heavy&quot; the use of multiple (always totally optional) books how you're defining it? I mean I get that from that point of view D&amp;D in all of its incarnations is relatively heavy because you need at least 2 of 3 core books to run it but I always found it to be rules lighter than Hero which has such a mathed out combat system that you basically play a miniatures board game every time combat happens. Personally I'm of the opinion that D&amp;D 3.5 and 2 are both (to use some boxing analogies) Super-middleweight systems compared to things like Rolemaster (Cruiserweight) and Hero System (Heavyweight). Compared to those systems CofD is a pretty svelt Middleweight system. Now D&amp;D 5 might be a Welterweight system .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I don't play start at 500 points like a lot people seem to play. Both as player and GM I try to avoid VPP's unless you can't build it no other way. And players with veep's damn well better have a rote setups. Non of this let's stop combat while min max a new setting in my variable power pool.<br /> <br /> What makes Champion hard is the presentation and its way of doing things. It is better to hand a newbie a copy of sidekick which has prebuilt templates that personalized then throwing the equivalent of assembler language for RPG's. Hero is really a meta rpg system where you have have assumptions in hand before you start as a GM. Not unlike GURPs. Now a preset campaign book like Tula Morn is more player friendly. Still I with right charts it child's play to build.<br /> <br /> Space Master with multiple stats (use this type int her, use that type of int there) while logical would throw a lot people off.<br /> Played Amber it is different. It is whole different style . Kind of help me with OWOD in a strange way.<br /> <br /> You want light weight try RISUS. I've been dinking with that lately.<br /> <br /> Now back to OP's problem Dice pools can be weird to someone not used using them. A lot people used to percentiles don't like hero's 3d6 system.<br /> Dead lands poker style is really weird to some. But it would help if OP spelled out what his group is having issues with and if they are using version 1 or 2.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:59:15-07:00","id":861274,"title":"","content":"True, true. When it comes to dice pools you can do a lot of substitutions. Of course I always assumed that some WoD / CofD (and FASA d6) fans simply liked the heft of all those dice. It's like craps on steroids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:08:00-07:00","id":861399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=860972#post860972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such as? It's cut down a bit, but nothing you really <i>need</i> is left out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've answered this before in a few other threads. Going to mostly quote myself with some additions:<br /> <br /> Foot chase rules (referenced in Parkour but not explained anywhere in the book)<br /> Falling/crashing rules (a player wanted to use Vigor to throw someone into a wall to deal damage, which Vigor is described as being able to do, but there's no rules for using people as damage. I ended up using Stamina as Durability for damage calculations)<br /> Size details (speed factor seems to = size now, so I'm not putting speed on this list)<br /> Strength scale (How much can you lift at each dot level? Important for Vigor)<br /> Cars and all the many, many rules that go with them in WoD core<br /> Example drugs (has come up at least twice in a dozen sessions and had to reference WoD Core)<br /> Teamwork Grappling (this is in the GMC update, though it leaves a bit to be desired, like how it works with initiative)<br /> Crafting (this can have some leeway, since it's never been core book material until the new CofD core anyway)<br /> Drug and disease rules for vampires (it's a straight copy/paste from the core for mortals; the rules for vampires require the FAQ/errata)<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's more I'm not thinking of right now, but this is just what came up in the course of actual play for me and my group. Most of it, I find, is pretty important for a vampire game. Foot chase in particular being referenced in the VtR 2e book but not included. I'd also include the expanded Blood Sorcery rules, since I find the ones included in the core to be largely useless, but that's more a matter of opinion. Also all the little fluff tidbits that Rose and other devs keep saying were once included but had to be removed for space concerns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:20:38-07:00","id":861406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=861399#post861399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength scale (How much can you lift at each dot level? Important for Vigor)</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I wrong or strength scale isn't there in the new core CofD? I miss it or Should I use the table in the oldWod core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:31:46-07:00","id":861411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854902-ire-and-the-rules?p=861406#post861406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I wrong or strength scale isn't there in the new core CofD? I miss it or Should I use the table in the oldWod core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't find it in the new CofD core, so you probably have to use the old 1e core book. Either way, it's not in VtR 2e core, which is kind of strange considering one of the uses of Vigor really requires it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:43:28-07:00","id":861422,"title":"","content":"Yes I agree on this. But it's even more strange that it isn't inside the CofD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T17:06:06-07:00","id":861439,"title":"","content":"There is a Size chart on p26 of the Chronicles of Darkness book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}